    {
      "startSec": 31.627,
      "endSec": 36.227,
      "heading": "What is a go-around?",
      "body": "A go-around means abandoning a landing and climbing away to try again. It is a routine, trained procedure, and controllers can order one when spacing or the runway isn't ready."
    },
    {
      "startSec": 58.487,
      "endSec": 63.087,
      "heading": "Wake turbulence",
      "body": "Large aircraft leave swirling air behind them. Controllers warn following pilots, especially behind heavy jets like a Boeing 777, so they can plan their approach accordingly."
    }
  ],
